Mr. Rasmuson,
Thank you for your op-ed addressing the serious fiscal challenges facing Alaska. Please note a few clarifications for the sake of accuracy:

1. Budget figures presented are inaccurate - actual state FY18 operating spend and deficit are $4.2b and $2.5b, respectively. These are in unrestricted general funds terms - which is the terminology consistently usedb y govt and the ADN to describe state finances;

2. Per SB 26 (POMV), a 5% draw would not translate into 5%, because SB26 uses a historical 5-year fund value averaging formula before making a draw, creating an smaller effective draw rate. Most endowments use this method to offset the effects of volatility - perhaps your foundation uses it too;

3. Absent a const. POMV, inflation-proofing is not automatic under SB26 and requires Leg action. But (spoiler alert) they haven't done it since FY16. Not inflation-proofing the PF is making your father's fear become a reality; and

4. The ERA is not the PF. See AS 37.13.145(a)

